# DKMS configuration for the Rust rewrite of the Loongson-3 CPUFreq driver.
#
# IMPORTANT: a *Rust* kernel module cannot be built the usual way from a
# linux-headers package.  It is compiled against the kernel's compiled Rust
# abstractions (rust/libkernel.rmeta, rust/libcore.rmeta, ...), which the
# headers package does not ship, and it has to use the exact rustc the kernel
# itself was built with, because Rust mangled symbol names embed a hash of the
# compiler.  `tools/setup-rfl.sh` prepares such a tree and `tools/rfl-env.sh`
# exports the matching environment.
#
# AUTOINSTALL is therefore deliberately left unset: DKMS registers the module
# but does not build it behind your back -- that would fail on a stock system
# and would be retried on every kernel upgrade.  Once a kernel tree has been
# prepared, build it with:
#
#     . /usr/src/loongson3-cpufreq-7.2.8/tools/rfl-env.sh
#     dkms build   loongson3-cpufreq/7.2.8 --kernelsourcedir="$KDIR"
#     dkms install loongson3-cpufreq/7.2.8 --kernelsourcedir="$KDIR"
#
# or simply
#
#     cd /usr/src/loongson3-cpufreq-7.2.8 && make && sudo make install

PACKAGE_NAME="loongson3-cpufreq"
PACKAGE_VERSION="#MODULE_VERSION#"
BUILT_MODULE_NAME[0]="loongson3_cpufreq"
DEST_MODULE_LOCATION[0]="/updates"
BUILD_EXCLUSIVE_ARCH="loongarch64"
